---

## 3️⃣ Full‑Featured Integration (Search, Auth, Private Tracks)

If you need **dynamic content** (search results, user‑specific playlists, private tracks) you’ll have to talk to the SoundCloud **REST API**. The flow is:

1. **Register a SoundCloud app** → get a **client_id** (and client_secret if you need OAuth).  
   *Go to https://soundcloud.com/you/apps → “Register a new application”.*  
2. **(Optional) Authenticate the user** if you want to play their private tracks or let them like/follow.  
3. **Search / fetch track metadata** → obtain the `track_id` and the **stream URL** (or just feed the ID to the widget).  
4. **Play** using the widget (recommended) or, for advanced use‑cases, use the **stream URL** with the HTML5 `<audio>` element (requires a valid OAuth token for private tracks).

Below is a minimal example that **searches for a keyword**, displays the first 5 results, and lets the visitor click a result to load it into the widget.

### 3.1 Get a client ID

```js
const CLIENT_ID = 'YOUR_CLIENT_ID_HERE'; // <-- replace with your own
```

### 3.2 Search function (uses the `searchContent` tool you have)

We’ll call the tool to fetch tracks matching a query.

```javascript
async function searchTracks(query, limit = 5) {
  const response = await fetch(`https://api.soundcloud.com/tracks?client_id=${CLIENT_ID}&q=${encodeURIComponent(query)}&limit=${limit}`);
  if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Search failed');
  return response.json(); // array of track objects
}
```

> **Note:** If you prefer to use the provided `searchContent` function (the sandboxed tool), you can call it like this:

```javascript
await searchContent({ query: 'lofi chill', limit: 5, type: 'track' });
```

The tool returns the same JSON structure you’d get from the public API.

### 3.3 Full HTML/JS example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>SoundCloud Search & Play</title>
  <script src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/api.js"></script>
  <style>
    body { font-family: sans-serif; max-width: 800px; margin: auto; }
    #results { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
    #results li { margin: 8px 0; cursor: pointer; }
    #results li:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>Search SoundCloud</h1>
<input id="searchBox" type="text" placeholder="Enter a keyword…" />
<button id="searchBtn">Search</button>

<ul id="results"></ul>

<h2>Now Playing</h2>
<div id="playerContainer"></div>

<script>
  const CLIENT_ID = 'YOUR_CLIENT_ID_HERE'; // <-- put your client id here

  const searchBox = document.getElementById('searchBox');
  const searchBtn = document.getElementById('searchBtn');
  const resultsUl = document.getElementById('results');
  const playerContainer = document.getElementById('playerContainer');

  let widget = null; // will hold the SC.Widget instance

  async function doSearch() {
    const query = searchBox.value.trim();
    if (!query) return;

    // 1️⃣ Call the public API (or the sandboxed tool)
    const tracks = await fetch(`https://api.soundcloud.com/tracks?client_id=${CLIENT_ID}&q=${encodeURIComponent(query)}&limit=10`)
      .then(r => r.json());

    // 2️⃣ Render results
    resultsUl.innerHTML = '';
    tracks.forEach(track => {
      const li = document.createElement('li');
      li.textContent = `${track.title} – ${track.user.username}`;
      li.dataset.id = track.id;
      li.onclick = () => loadTrack(track.id);
      resultsUl.appendChild(li);
    });
  }

  function loadTrack(trackId) {
    // Build the widget URL
    const src = `https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=${encodeURIComponent('https://api.soundcloud.com/tracks/' + trackId)}&color=%23ff5500&auto_play=true&visual=true`;

    // If we already have an iframe, just change its src; otherwise create it.
    let iframe = playerContainer.querySelector('iframe');
    if (!iframe) {
      iframe = document.createElement('iframe');
      iframe.setAttribute('allow', 'autoplay');
      iframe.setAttribute('scrolling', 'no');
      iframe.setAttribute('frameborder', 'no');
      iframe.width = '100%';
      iframe.height = '300';
      playerContainer.appendChild(iframe);
    }
    iframe.src = src;

    // (Re)create the widget object
    widget = SC.Widget(iframe);
  }

  // Hook up UI
  searchBtn.onclick = doSearch;
  searchBox.addEventListener('keypress', e => {
    if (e.key === 'Enter') doSearch();
  });
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

**What you get**

* A search box that queries SoundCloud for the entered keyword.
* A list of the first 10 matching tracks.
* Clicking a result loads that track into a **widget player** that starts playing automatically.

### 3.4 Authenticating a user (OAuth)

If you need to let users log in (e.g., to play their private tracks, like songs, or create playlists), follow these steps:

1. **Redirect the user to the SoundCloud auth endpoint**

```html
<a href="https://soundcloud.com/connect?client_id=YOUR_CLIENT_ID&redirect_uri=YOUR_CALLBACK_URL&response_type=code&scope=non-expiring">
  Log in with SoundCloud
</a>
```

2. **Handle the callback** – SoundCloud will redirect to `YOUR_CALLBACK_URL?code=AUTH_CODE`. Exchange that code for an access token:

```bash
POST https://api.soundcloud.com/oauth2/token
  client_id=YOUR_CLIENT_ID
  client_secret=YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET
  grant_type=authorization_code
  redirect_uri=YOUR_CALLBACK_URL
  code=AUTH_CODE
```

3. **Store the `access_token`** (usually in a secure HTTP‑only cookie or server‑side session).  
   Use it for any API call that requires user authentication:

```js
fetch(`https://api.soundcloud.com/me?oauth_token=${access_token}`)
  .then(r => r.json())
  .then(user => console.log('Logged in as', user.username));
```

4. **Play private tracks** – the widget can accept an `oauth_token` parameter:

```html
<iframe src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=https%3A//api.soundcloud.com/tracks/PRIVATE_TRACK_ID&oauth_token=USER_ACCESS_TOKEN&auto_play=true"></iframe>
```

> **Tip:** For most public playback scenarios you **don’t need OAuth**; a client‑id is enough. Only request the `non‑expiring` scope if you truly need a long‑lived token.

---

## 4️⃣ Common Gotchas & Best Practices

| Issue | Why it happens | Fix / Recommendation |
|-------|----------------|-----------------------|
| **CORS errors when fetching stream URLs directly** | SoundCloud blocks cross‑origin streaming for most browsers unless you use the widget or an authenticated request. | **Never** embed the raw `stream_url` in an `<audio>` tag unless you have a valid OAuth token and the proper `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header. Use the widget instead. |
| **Rate‑limit (client_id) exceeded** | Public client IDs are limited to ~15,000 requests per hour. | Cache results, request only what you need, and consider applying for a **commercial API key** if you expect high traffic. |
| **Track is not streamable** | Some tracks are “download only” or blocked in certain regions. | The API returns `streamable: false`. Filter those out or show a friendly “unavailable” message. |
| **Widget height mismatch** | The visual player (`visual=true`) is 450 px tall, while the classic player is 166 px. | Set the iframe height accordingly (`height="450"` for visual, `height="166"` for classic). |
| **Mobile autoplay blocked** | Mobile browsers block autoplay unless the user has interacted with the page. | Call `widget.play()` only after a user click (e.g., a “Play” button). |
| **OAuth token expires** | Tokens can be short‑lived unless you request the `non‑expiring` scope. | Store the token securely and refresh it via the `/oauth2/token` endpoint if you didn’t request a non‑expiring token. |

---

## 5️⃣ TL;DR – Minimal Code to Drop Into Any Page

```html
