  const src = `https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=${encodeURIComponent('https://api.soundcloud.com/tracks/' + TRACK_ID)}&color=%23ff5500&auto_play=false&visual=true`;

  // Insert the iframe
  const iframe = document.createElement('iframe');
  iframe.setAttribute('allow', 'autoplay');
  iframe.setAttribute('scrolling', 'no');
  iframe.setAttribute('frameborder', 'no');
  iframe.width = '100%';
  iframe.height = '450';   // visual player height
  iframe.src = src;
  document.getElementById('sc-player').appendChild(iframe);

  // Optional: expose a simple JS API
  const widget = SC.Widget(iframe);
  window.scPlay = () => widget.play();
  window.scPause = () => widget.pause();
</script>

<!-- Example buttons -->
<button onclick="scPlay()">Play</button>
<button onclick="scPause()">Pause</button>
```

Copy‑paste the snippet, replace `TRACK_ID` with the ID of the track you want, and you’re live.

---

## 6️⃣ Next Steps for You

1. **Create a SoundCloud developer app** → get `client_id` (and `client_secret` if you need OAuth).  
2. Decide which integration level you need (embed vs. widget vs. full SDK).  
3. Implement the code snippet that matches your needs.  
4. Test on both desktop and mobile browsers (pay attention to autoplay restrictions).  
5. (Optional) Add a **search UI** using the `searchContent` tool you have, so visitors can discover tracks on the fly.  

