### What a “Callback URL” (Redirect URI) Is

When you use SoundCloud’s OAuth flow the user is sent to **SoundCloud’s login/authorization page**.  
After the user grants (or denies) permission, SoundCloud sends the browser back to a URL **you control** and appends an authorization code (or an error) to the query string:

```
https://your‑site.com/soundcloud/callback?code=AUTH_CODE
```

That URL is called the **callback URL** (or **redirect URI**).  
Your server reads the `code` parameter, exchanges it for an **access token**, stores the token (usually in a session or a secure cookie), and then redirects the user to the final page of your app (e.g., a dashboard, player page, etc.).

---

## 1️⃣ Choosing a Callback URL

| Situation | Recommended URL | Why |
|-----------|----------------|-----|
| **Production website** | `https://www.yourdomain.com/auth/soundcloud/callback` | Must be a **public HTTPS** address that you own. |
| **Development on localhost** | `http://localhost:3000/auth/soundcloud/callback` (or any port you run your dev server on) | SoundCloud allows `http://localhost` for testing, but **never** use plain‑http on a real domain. |
| **Single‑page app (SPA) that handles the code client‑side** | `https://app.yourdomain.com/` (the same page that initiates the login) – you’ll read `window.location.search` to get `code`. | The page can parse the query string and then call your back‑end to exchange the code. |
| **Serverless / Netlify / Vercel functions** | `https://my‑site.netlify.app/.netlify/functions/soundcloud-callback` | The function endpoint can process the code and return a JSON response or redirect. |

**Key rules**

1. **Exact match** – The URL you register in the SoundCloud app settings **must** match exactly (including protocol, sub‑domain, path, and trailing slash).  
2. **HTTPS for production** – SoundCloud requires HTTPS for any non‑localhost domain.  
3. **One URL per app** (you can add multiple by separating them with commas in the SoundCloud dashboard, but each must be listed).  

---

## 2️⃣ How to Register the Callback URL in the SoundCloud Developer Console

1. Go to **https://soundcloud.com/you/apps** (replace *you* with your username).  
2. Click the app you created (or “Create a new app” if you haven’t).  
3. In the **OAuth Settings** section you’ll see fields:  

   - **Redirect URI** (or “Callback URL”) – paste the URL you decided on.  
   - **Scope** – leave as `*` unless you need a more limited set.  

4. Click **Save**.

> **Tip:** If you later need to add another environment (e.g., a staging server), just edit the app again and add the new URL separated by a comma.

---

## 3️⃣ Minimal End‑to‑End Example

Below is a **complete, runnable example** using **Node.js + Express** (you can adapt it to any backend language). It shows:

1. A **login button** that redirects the user to SoundCloud’s auth page.  
2. A **callback route** (`/auth/soundcloud/callback`) that receives the `code`.  
3. The **token‑exchange** request (POST to `https://api.soundcloud.com/oauth2/token`).  
4. Storing the token in a server‑side session and finally redirecting the user to a protected page.

### 3.1 Project Setup (Node)

```bash
mkdir sc-demo && cd sc-demo
npm init -y
npm install express express-session node-fetch
```

### 3.2 `server.js`

```js
// server.js
require('dotenv').config();          // optional: load .env file
const express = require('express');
const session = require('express-session');
const fetch   = require('node-fetch');
const app = express();
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;

// -------------------------------------------------
// 1️⃣  Configuration – fill these in (or put in .env)
// -------------------------------------------------
const CLIENT_ID     = process.env.SOUNDCLOUD_CLIENT_ID;      // <-- your client id
const CLIENT_SECRET = process.env.SOUNDCLOUD_CLIENT_SECRET;  // <-- your client secret
const REDIRECT_URI  = process.env.SOUNDCLOUD_REDIRECT_URI;   // <-- e.g. http://localhost:3000/auth/soundcloud/callback

if (!CLIENT_ID || !CLIENT_SECRET || !REDIRECT_URI) {
  console.error('❌  Missing SoundCloud credentials – set them in .env or env vars');
  process.exit(1);
}

// -------------------------------------------------
// 2️⃣  Session middleware (stores the access token)
// -------------------------------------------------
app.use(session({
  secret: 'a‑very‑random‑string‑change‑me',
  resave: false,
  saveUninitialized: true,
  cookie: { secure: false }   // set true if you serve over HTTPS
}));

// -------------------------------------------------
// 3️⃣  Home page – shows a login button or player
// -------------------------------------------------
app.get('/', (req, res) => {
  const loggedIn = !!req.session.scAccessToken;
  res.send(`
    <h1>SoundCloud OAuth Demo</h1>
    ${loggedIn
      ? `<p>✅ Logged in! <a href="/player">Go to player</a> | <a href="/logout">Log out</a></p>`
      : `<a href="/auth/soundcloud"><button>Log in with SoundCloud</button></a>`
    }
  `);
});

// -------------------------------------------------
// 4️⃣  Initiate OAuth – redirect user to SoundCloud
// -------------------------------------------------
app.get('/auth/soundcloud', (req, res) => {
  const authUrl = new URL('https://soundcloud.com/connect');
  authUrl.searchParams.set('client_id', CLIENT_ID);
  authUrl.searchParams.set('redirect_uri', REDIRECT_URI);
  authUrl.searchParams.set('response_type', 'code');
  authUrl.searchParams.set('scope', '*');          // you can limit if you wish
  authUrl.searchParams.set('display', 'popup');   // optional
  res.redirect(authUrl.toString());
});

// -------------------------------------------------
// 5️⃣  Callback – SoundCloud sends ?code=…
// -------------------------------------------------
app.get('/auth/soundcloud/callback', async (req, res) => {
  const { code, error } = req.query;

  if (error) {
    return res.send(`❌  SoundCloud error: ${error}`);
  }
  if (!code) {
    return res.send('❌  No authorization code received.');
  }

  // Exchange the code for an access token
  try {
    const tokenResp = await fetch('https://api.soundcloud.com/oauth2/token', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' },
      body: new URLSearchParams({
        client_id: CLIENT_ID,
        client_secret: CLIENT_SECRET,
        grant_type: 'authorization_code',
        redirect_uri: REDIRECT_URI,
        code
      })
    });

    const tokenData = await tokenResp.json();

    if (tokenData.error) {
      return res.send(`❌  Token error: ${tokenData.error_description || tokenData.error}`);
    }

    // Store token (and optionally refresh_token) in the session
    req.session.scAccessToken = tokenData.access_token;
    req.session.scRefreshToken = tokenData.refresh_token; // may be undefined if you didn't request non‑expiring
    req.session.scUserId = tokenData.user_id;

    // Redirect to a protected page (e.g., player)
    res.redirect('/player');
  } catch (e) {
    console.error(e);
    res.send('❌  Failed to exchange code for token.');
  }
});

// -------------------------------------------------
// 6️⃣  Simple protected page that shows the user’s name
// -------------------------------------------------
app.get('/player', async (req, res) => {
  if (!req.session.scAccessToken) {
    return res.redirect('/');
  }

  // Fetch the logged‑in user’s profile (just to prove the token works)
  const userResp = await fetch(`https://api.soundcloud.com/me?oauth_token=${req.session.scAccessToken}`);
  const user = await userResp.json();

  // Render a tiny widget player for a demo track (replace with any track ID)
  const demoTrackId = '13158665'; // “Lofi Hip Hop Radio – Beats to Relax/Study to”
  const widgetUrl = `https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=${encodeURIComponent('https://api.soundcloud.com/tracks/' + demoTrackId)}&auto_play=false&visual=true`;

  res.send(`
    <h1>Hello, ${user.username}!</h1>
    <p>Here’s a SoundCloud widget that will play using your OAuth token (so private tracks would also work).</p>
    <iframe
      id="sc-widget"
      width="100%" height="450"
      scrolling="no" frameborder="no"
      allow="autoplay"
      src="${widgetUrl}&oauth_token=${req.session.scAccessToken}">
    </iframe>
    <br/>
    <a href="/logout"><button>Log out</button></a>
  `);
});

// -------------------------------------------------
// 7️⃣  Log out – clear session
// -------------------------------------------------
app.get('/logout', (req, res) => {
  req.session.destroy(() => res.redirect('/'));
});

app.listen(PORT, () => console.log(`🚀  Server listening on http://localhost:${PORT}`));
```

#### `.env` (keep this file out of version control)

```
SOUNDCLOUD_CLIENT_ID=YOUR_CLIENT_ID
SOUNDCLOUD_CLIENT_SECRET=YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET
SOUNDCLOUD_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/auth/soundcloud/callback
```

**Run it**

```bash
node server.js
```

Open `http://localhost:3000` → click **Log in with SoundCloud** → you’ll be taken to SoundCloud, approve the app, and be redirected back to `/auth/soundcloud/callback`. After the token exchange you land on `/player` where the widget plays a track using your OAuth token.

