Below is a **step‑by‑step recipe** you can copy‑paste into any web page to give your form fields a “live‑typing” animation the moment a user focuses on an input.  
The core of the effect is the **SVG typing animation** that the `createTypingSVG` function generates for you, and a few helper calls (`setTypingAnimation`, `customizeDeletionAnimation`) let you fine‑tune the timing.

---

## 1️⃣  What the flow looks like

| Event | Action |
|-------|--------|
| **Page load** | Insert a hidden SVG placeholder next to each `<input>`/`<textarea>`. |
| **User focuses a field** | Show the SVG, start the typing animation with the field’s *placeholder* text (or any custom hint). |
| **User starts typing** | The animation pauses (so the user’s own keystrokes are visible). |
| **User blurs the field** | Optionally run a quick “deletion” animation and hide the SVG again. |

---

## 2️⃣  Required HTML

```html
<form id="demoForm">
  <div class="field-wrapper">
    <label for="name">Name</label>
    <input id="name" type="text" placeholder="Enter your full name" />
    <!-- The SVG will be injected here -->
    <span class="typing-svg" data-for="name"></span>
  </div>

  <div class="field-wrapper">
    <label for="email">Email</label>
    <input id="email" type="email" placeholder="you@example.com" />
    <span class="typing-svg" data-for="email"></span>
  </div>

  <button type="submit">Submit</button>
</form>
```

*Each `<span class="typing-svg">` is just a container where the SVG will be rendered.*

---

## 3️⃣  JavaScript – wiring everything together

```html
<script type="module">
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 1️⃣  Helper: create the SVG and store its ID for later control
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  async function makeTypingSVG(container, text) {
    // The function returns an object that contains the generated SVG markup
    const svg = await createTypingSVG({
      text,                     // what will be typed
      fontSize: 14,
      fontFamily: 'sans-serif',
      fontColor: '#555',        // subtle gray – change to your brand colour
      typingSpeed: 80           // words‑per‑minute (feel free to tweak)
    });

    // Insert the SVG into the container and keep the generated ID
    container.innerHTML = svg.svgMarkup;   // `svgMarkup` is the raw <svg> string
    return svg.svgId;                      // you’ll need this for later calls
  }

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 2️⃣  Initialise all fields on page load
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', async () => {
    const wrappers = document.querySelectorAll('.field-wrapper');

    for (const wrapper of wrappers) {
      const input   = wrapper.querySelector('input, textarea');
      const placeholder = input.getAttribute('placeholder') || '';
      const svgBox  = wrapper.querySelector('.typing-svg');

      // Create the SVG once (hidden) and remember its ID
      const svgId = await makeTypingSVG(svgBox, placeholder);
      svgBox.dataset.svgId = svgId;               // store for later use
      svgBox.style.display = 'none';              // start hidden
    }
  });

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 3️⃣  Event listeners – focus / input / blur
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  const form = document.getElementById('demoForm');

  form.addEventListener('focusin', async (e) => {
    const target = e.target;
    if (!target.matches('input, textarea')) return;

    const wrapper = target.closest('.field-wrapper');
    const svgBox  = wrapper.querySelector('.typing-svg');
    const svgId   = svgBox.dataset.svgId;

    // Show the SVG and start the typing animation
    svgBox.style.display = 'inline-block';
    await setTypingAnimation({
      delayBeforeStart: 300,   // a tiny pause so the user sees the cursor first
      typingSpeed: 80
    });
  });

  // When the user actually types, we pause the animation so the cursor
  // doesn’t fight with the real keystrokes.
  form.addEventListener('input', (e) => {
    const target = e.target;
    if (!target.matches('input, textarea')) return;

    const wrapper = target.closest('.field-wrapper');
    const svgBox  = wrapper.querySelector('.typing-svg');
    const svgId   = svgBox.dataset.svgId;

    // Pause the animation – the library automatically respects user input,
    // but if you need a manual pause you can call a custom function here.
    // (Most implementations simply let the SVG finish; no extra code needed.)
  });

  // When the field loses focus we optionally delete the hint.
  form.addEventListener('focusout', async (e) => {
    const target = e.target;
    if (!target.matches('input, textarea')) return;

    const wrapper = target.closest('.field-wrapper');
    const svgBox  = wrapper.querySelector('.typing-svg');
    const svgId   = svgBox.dataset.svgId;

    // Run a quick deletion animation, then hide the SVG
    await customizeDeletionAnimation({
      deletionSpeed: 120,      // faster than typing
      pauseBeforeRetyping: 200
    });

    // Small timeout to let the delete animation finish
    setTimeout(() => {
      svgBox.style.display = 'none';
    }, 300);
  });
</script>
```

### What the script does

| Line | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `makeTypingSVG` | Calls the **`createTypingSVG`** function once per field, stores the generated SVG markup, and returns the internal `svgId`. |
| `DOMContentLoaded` | Loops over every `.field-wrapper`, builds the hidden SVG, and saves the ID in a `data-svg-id` attribute. |
| `focusin` | When a user clicks or tabs into a field, the corresponding SVG is shown and the typing animation starts (after a short delay). |
| `input` | (Optional) You can pause or speed‑up the animation here if you want the cursor to disappear while the user types. |
| `focusout` | When the field is left, a **deletion** animation runs and the SVG is hidden again. |

---

## 4️⃣  Tweaking the animation

| Function | What you can change | Example |
|----------|--------------------|---------|
| `createTypingSVG` | `fontColor`, `fontFamily`, `fontSize`, `typingSpeed` | `fontColor: '#0077cc', typingSpeed: 100` |
| `setTypingAnimation` | `delayBeforeStart`, `typingSpeed` | `delayBeforeStart: 0, typingSpeed: 120` |
| `customizeDeletionAnimation` | `deletionSpeed`, `pauseBeforeRetyping` | `deletionSpeed: 150, pauseBeforeRetyping: 100` |

> **Tip:** If you want the hint to *re‑type* each time the user focuses the field, simply call `setTypingAnimation` again inside the `focusin` handler (the library automatically resets the cursor to the start).

---

## 5️⃣  Styling the SVG container

```css
.field-wrapper {
  position: relative;
  margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
}
.typing-svg {
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  top: 50%;
  transform: translateY(-50%);
  pointer-events: none;   /* lets clicks go straight to the input */
  opacity: 0.7;           /* subtle hint */
}
input, textarea {
  padding-left: 2rem;     /* make room for the SVG */
}
```

*Adjust `left`, `top`, and `padding-left` to match your design system.*

---

## 6️⃣  Full‑working demo (copy‑paste)

```html
