  .typing-svg { position:absolute; left:8px; top:50%; transform:translateY(-50%); pointer-events:none; opacity:0.6; }
  input, textarea { width:100%; padding:8px 8px 8px 30px; font-size:14px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<form id="demoForm">
  <div class="field-wrapper">
    <label for="name">Name</label>
    <input id="name" placeholder="Enter your full name">
    <span class="typing-svg" data-for="name"></span>
  </div>

  <div class="field-wrapper">
    <label for="email">Email</label>
    <input id="email" placeholder="you@example.com">
    <span class="typing-svg" data-for="email"></span>
  </div>

  <button type="submit">Submit</button>
</form>

<script type="module">
  // (Paste the JavaScript from section 3️⃣ here)
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

Open the file in a browser, click into a field, and you’ll see the placeholder text being “typed” out in real time.

---

## 7️⃣  Going further

| Idea | How to implement |
|------|------------------|
| **Multiple hints per field** (e.g., “First name”, “Last name”) | Store an array of strings and on each `focusin` pick the next one, then call `updateTypingSVG` to change the text without recreating the SVG. |
| **Responsive speed** (slow on mobile, fast on desktop) | Detect `navigator.maxTouchPoints` or screen width and pass a different `typingSpeed` to `setTypingAnimation`. |
| **Accessibility** – hide the SVG from screen readers | Add `aria-hidden="true"` to the `<svg>` element (the library does this automatically, but you can double‑check). |
| **Custom cursor** (blinking block vs. vertical bar) | Change the SVG’s CSS: `svg .cursor { stroke:#0077cc; }` or inject a `<style>` tag inside the generated markup. |

---

### TL;DR

1. **Create a hidden SVG** for each input with `createTypingSVG`.  
2. **Show it on focus** and start the animation with `setTypingAnimation`.  
3. **Optionally delete** on blur using `customizeDeletionAnimation`.  
4. **Style** the container so the SVG sits nicely inside the input field.

That’s all you need to give users a smooth, “live‑typing” cue that makes form‑filling feel interactive and polished. Happy coding! 🚀

